**Council guidance on outbuildings**
Garden rooms and sheds that are under 2.5 metres high, sit behind the front wall of the house, and cover less than half the garden do not usually need an application. The conservation area status means this general rule may not apply to you, so you should check before building.

**Next steps**
- Measure the building's maximum height and check whether it would sit behind the front wall of the house. Also estimate what share of the garden it would cover.
- If it's over 2.5 metres, in front of the house, or would take up more than half the garden, you will probably need an application.
- Even if it falls within the general guidance, the conservation area may require an application. Contact the planning desk to confirm before you start work.

